--- !u!114 &1887391713
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1887391711}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\u201CStop. I can\u2019t walk anymore.\u201D\n\nJames turned around when
    he heard Maddie\u2019s pained groan.\n\nHe realised that she had fallen quite
    far behind. She was leaning against the handrail, her body slumped against it.\n\nHer
    raincoat was a bright yellow, almost exactly the same colour as an American school
    bus. Ducks wearing sunglasses and holding inflatable rings were printed all over
    it, making the design seem a little childish for a woman in her twenties.\n\n\n\n\n\nThen
    again, James himself had packed a raincoat in his backpack just in case. The
    forecast for today had called for cloudy skies with no rain, but since they were
    visiting Japan, he had decided that being prepared for any kind of weather was
    the more sensible choice.\n\nOther tourists passed by Maddie as she stood there,
    breathing heavily and looking exhausted.\n\n\u201CCome on, you can do it. We\u2019ve
    only just started climbing the stairs,\u201D Liam teased her from further up
    the steps, ahead of James.\n\nThe three of them had come to Japan from the Gold
    Coast in Australia, and it had already been three days since they arrived.\n\nOn
    their first day, they had gone around buying up the strong liquor they had heard
    so much about from convenience stores. On the second day, they had spent almost
    the entire day sleeping in their hotel rooms with terrible hangovers.\n\nSo,
    for the three of them, who had barely experienced Japan at all despite it being
    their first visit, today was finally a proper day of sightseeing.\n\nThis temple
    in Kyoto was famous for its hundreds of torii gates standing one after another,
    and it was normally expected to be crowded with tourists. Fortunately, however,
    there was apparently a special festival taking place in town today, so there
    were surprisingly few people around.\n\nThe sound of festival music could be
    heard somewhere in the distance.\n\nA cold gust of wind suddenly swept past them,
    unusually chilly for September.\n\nThe sun looked as though it would set in less
    than an hour.\n\n\u201CCome on. Let\u2019s make it to the top before it gets
    dark.\u201D\n\n\u201CYou two are trying to kill me, aren\u2019t you? Seriously,
    there are way too many stairs in Japan.\u201D\n\nMaddie cursed under her breath
    as she took another step, her blonde hair"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 84eca623474ae7e4588f602ba2c56199, type: 2}
